    methodology: 'A prospective study of one reporting cycle. Each material status claim is linked to its governing milestone definition, source records, source timestamps, conflict note, owner response, published wording, and later correction. GAO data-reliability guidance frames accuracy, completeness, and applicability; NIST governance concepts frame role ownership and retained evidence. The method diagnoses reporting reliability, not team performance or delivery probability.',
